.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

int bc_pty_resize(bc_client_t *c, int rows, int cols);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resizes the active PTY session\(cqs terminal to \f[B]rows\f[R] x
\f[B]cols\f[R].
The server applies \f[CR]TIOCSWINSZ\f[R] to the PTY master file
descriptor and sends \f[CR]SIGWINCH\f[R] to the child process group,
notifying terminal\- aware applications (such as editors, pagers, and
shells) of the dimension change.
.PP
A PTY session must have been previously spawned with
\f[CR]bc_pty_spawn(3)\f[R].
If no PTY session is active, this function returns
\f[CR]BC_ERR_PROTOCOL\f[R].
.SH Wire protocol
Sends on \f[CR]CHAN_PTY\f[R] (channel 5):
.IP
.EX
{\(dqaction\(dq:\(dqresize\(dq,\(dqrows\(dq:40,\(dqcols\(dq:120}
.EE
.PP
Receives acknowledgement:
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqresized\(dq,\(dqrows\(dq:40,\(dqcols\(dq:120}
.EE
